Docker Compose manages multi-container applications defined in YAML configuration files.

Start all services defined in the Docker Compose file
#docker compose up

Start services in detached background mode
#docker compose up -d

Rebuild images before starting services
#docker compose up --build

Stop and remove containers and networks
#docker compose down

Stop services and also remove volumes
#docker compose down -v

List running Docker Compose services
#docker compose ps

View logs for all services
#docker compose logs

Follow logs of a specific service in real time
#docker compose logs -f <service_name>

Open a bash shell inside a running service container
#docker compose exec <service_name> bash

Run a one time command in a service
#docker compose run <service_name> <command>

Build or rebuild service images
#docker compose build

Pull images for all services
#docker compose pull

Restart all services
#docker compose restart

Stop services without removing them
#docker compose stop

Validate and display the merged Compose configuration
#docker compose config

Scale a service to multiple instances
#docker compose scale <service_name>=<number_of_instances>

